      },
      "text": "Rope is the oldest manufactured composite material. Every major civilization independently developed spinning and twisting techniques. The fundamental constraint — only plant and animal fibers available until 1938 — shaped everything: the maximum strength achievable, the maintenance requirements, and the strategic importance of fiber supply."
    },
